  "parent_sha256": "037A69269671D8F487FA2269630B68351767623AB845A41BE4577ABBDF730A16",
  "status": "Tested on road in paired-20261105-150046-e5d55c90-v036-forrealsies; thermal protection confirmed (0.0F ECT rise), but low-RPM spool delayed by 2.0s due to retarded IVC at 2000-3500 RPM. Superseded by v037.",
  "rationale": "Derived from paired-20261105-104453-2eb3afbb-v035 telemetry review, confirmed engine build specs (85.5mm forged pistons, ~2.02L displacement, 9.25:1 static CR), and owner-requested high-RPM lockout: (1) In [ECM] 44412 (VCT Angle vs. RPM vs. Load), rows 0.70, 0.80, and 1.00 previously commanded up to -49.50 deg advance under boost, blowing 1,500 deg F pre-turbine exhaust gas backwards into intake runners. Candidate v036 zeros out boost rows 0.70-1.00 across all columns (1,000-7,200 RPM). (2) High-RPM transition lockout: because boost onset at 4k+ RPM is instantaneous and phaser hydraulic slew rate takes 200-300 ms to retard, columns 4,500 through 7,200 RPM are set to 0.00 deg across ALL loads (0.10 to 1.00). This pre-parks the cam at base timing across the entire powerband, eliminating transient shift reversion during gear changes. (3) 1,000-2,500 RPM retains smooth cruise advance (-10 to -35 deg) for off-boost spool and highway fuel economy, with 3,500 RPM tapered smoothly (-10 to -25 deg max). (4) Retains all v035 MBT spark timing (Row 9 13.5 deg flat across 5,500-7,200 RPM), v035 WOT base fuel enleanment (0.76-0.77 lambda), v033 loud decel crackle, and v032 anti-shuffle fixes.",
